{
  "schema_version": 1,
  "_doctrine": "The Youngevity Product-DB nutrient/ingredient registry (Pillar 3, rebuilt in Phase F; the too-basic Phase-B nutrients.json was deleted 2026-07-05, then rebuilt RICHER here). Three parts, none derivable in full from a single pillar: (1) essential_aliases -- which product-label vitamin/mineral name credits which of the 91 essentials (essentials-canon slugs); (2) canonical_forms -- the collision-collapse map (norm-key -> ONE canonical display form) that unifies label-faithful surface variants (Ginkgo biloba/Ginkgo Biloba, L-glutamine/L-Glutamine) so aggregation + search group correctly; (3) nutrients -- the pre-registered substance vocabulary (every corpus other_substances slug), which RE-LIGHTS the dormant substance half of references_resolve (a claim can no longer cite a phantom substance). display_name mirrors corpus_derive.humanize(slug) so the derived other-substances index stays byte-identical; canon_slug is null (other_substances are non-essential by the corpus's own essentials/other split). Minerals/amino acids matching a canon display_name, and fatty acids by omega family, resolve by RULE in nutrient_resolve.py. The products pillar stays byte-faithful to the labels; canonicalization lives HERE (registry layer), never lossily in-pillar. Composition-only (SS00.A): nothing here is a Wallach target.",
